{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Two units have zero production references, confirmed symbol-by-symbol including the reconciler's\ndynamic `_load()`-by-filename seam, and independently re-verified by a blue-team pass.\n\n**`bug_close_reason_ok`** (`_commands/txn.py:154-160`) — zero callers repo-wide. Its docstring\nactively lies: \"Shared by `transition_core`'s close guard and the completion gate's pre-check... so\nthe two cannot drift.\" Both consumers migrated to `bug_close_class_ok` (`txn.py:262`,\n`close_precheck.py:183`), whose sibling docstring makes the identical claim truthfully. A reader\nauditing the close guard finds two near-identical \"shared anti-drift guard\" functions and can pick\nthe dead one, reintroducing free-text validation into a path that enforces a bounded enum.\n\n**`_engine/rebar_reconciler/_attestation.py`** — the WHOLE module (126 LOC, three symbols:\n`verify_manifest_hash:16`, `build_acli_client_from_env:41`, `verify_attested_commit:72`), kept alive\nonly by its own ~200-line unit test and carried through unrelated refactors. A GPG-signature-verifying\ngate that is tested, maintained, and never invoked is a false assurance signal.\n`adapters/jira/backend.py:192` still claims the adapter \"Preserves the pre-97f2\n`build_acli_client_from_env` contract\", implying a live partner that does not exist.\n\nFlagged in the 2026-07-07 audit and unremediated since.\n\nCASCADE: consider caller + dynamic-reference (reflection / string dispatch / DI / dynamic import)\nimpact. The reconciler's dynamic loader was already cleared during verification.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `bug_close_reason_ok` is deleted; `bug_close_class_ok`'s docstring is the only anti-drift claim\n- [ ] `_engine/rebar_reconciler/_attestation.py` and its unit test are deleted\n- [ ] The dangling contract claim at `adapters/jira/backend.py:192` is corrected\n- [ ] Each deletion is a separate commit so either can be reverted independently\n\n## CORRECTION (plan-review BLOCK, criteria E4/G1G2/G6) — the consumer set was wrong\n\nThe paragraph above said `_attestation.py` is \"kept alive only by its own ~200-line unit\ntest\". That is FALSE, and verified so against the tree. There are THREE consumers, and a\ndeletion that removes only the unit test leaves a broken suite:\n\n1. `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_attestation.py` — the known unit test. It loads the\n   module BY PATH (`ATTESTATION_PATH = .../rebar_reconciler/_attestation.py`, `:27`) via\n   `importlib.util.spec_from_file_location` (`:31`).\n2. `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_config_jira_wiring.py:217,226,233` — a config-routing\n   test for ticket 0ac6. It does `from rebar_reconciler import _attestation` and calls\n   `_attestation.build_acli_client_from_env()`. This is an UNENUMERATED consumer with nothing to\n   do with attestation testing; deleting the module breaks it.\n3. `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_backend_neutrality.py:42,147` — two parametrized guard\n   tuples (`_NO_INLINE_ACLICLIENT`, `_ZERO_ADAPTER_IMPORT_SCALAR_CORE`) list the string\n   `\"_attestation.py\"` and `read_text()` each path. Deleting the file makes those cases raise\n   `FileNotFoundError` rather than pass.\n\nConsumers 2 and 3 are exactly the class the repo's own navigation guidance warns about: a\nsymbol/file named AS A STRING, which semantic search does not surface. The original CASCADE note\ncleared the reconciler's dynamic `_load()` seam but did not grep for the filename as a string.\n\nThis does not overturn the deletion — no PRODUCTION module imports `_attestation`, so the\n\"tested, maintained, never invoked\" finding stands. It changes the MECHANISM.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria (supersedes the list above for the `_attestation` half)\n\n- [ ] `bug_close_reason_ok` is deleted; `bug_close_class_ok`'s docstring is the only anti-drift claim\n- [ ] `_engine/rebar_reconciler/_attestation.py` is deleted, together with ALL THREE consumers\n      handled: its unit test deleted; `test_config_jira_wiring.py`'s use of\n      `build_acli_client_from_env` re-pointed or removed with its intent (0ac6 config routing)\n      preserved by another assertion; and `\"_attestation.py\"` removed from BOTH guard tuples in\n      `test_backend_neutrality.py`\n- [ ] `grep -rn '_attestation' tests/ src/` returns no live reference after the change\n- [ ] The dangling contract claim at `adapters/jira/backend.py:192` is corrected\n- [ ] Each deletion is a separate commit so either can be reverted independently\n"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786077782721183001,"uuid":"c788a988-c589-4b23-b12e-433c44c16e2d"}